Allow terminal prompts on the exec connection

Allow rumpel exec -t/--tty to run programs that need a controlling
terminal, including SSH password prompts, without another container exec
or a terminal setup roundtrip. Keep enter behavior unchanged.

Carry terminal dimensions and TERM in the initial request, and forward
resizes independently of stdin so a blocked paste cannot stall redraws.
Use the local input or output terminal for size and resize events.
Restore local terminal settings after completion or errors. Combine
terminal stdout and stderr, preserving pipe behavior without --tty.

Forward external signals to foreground terminal jobs and clean up the
session's job groups when the client disconnects.
Allocate descriptors with atomic close-on-exec to keep concurrent
commands from inheriting each other's terminals.
Handle terminal hangup during blocked input so completed commands can
still deliver their output and exit status.

Cover password echo suppression, single-byte input, resize, Ctrl-C,
Ctrl-D, exit status, cleanup, and reuse of the existing pod connection.
Exercise scrollback and a real pager, including local dimensions with
redirected input and resizing while input is blocked.
